Now, to be fair, 99% of the population have from time to time symptoms that look a lot like OCD. The difference is the dimensionality of it. So we all occasionally, and for very good reasons, check things, try to keep things in order, wash. And these things are normative. And so when someone says, I have a little bit of OCD, the answer really is, of course you do, because that's a consequence of being alive. Well, Ms. Chatterjee, you volunteer as an advocate for the International OCD Foundation to raise awareness and educate the public about OCD. Do you encounter these myths in the work that you do every day? And how do you respond?
