myths and misconceptions. But I think the biggest one is that people with OCD like what they're doing. So when people say, I'm so OCD about cleaning or I'm so OCD about ordering things or about things being perfect, number one, that's again, syntactically incorrect. But number two, also, it's implying that I like something a certain way and I need it that way because I really, really like it. And people with OCD hate what they're doing. They do not want to be doing what they're doing. they do not want to be thinking about what they're doing, it is not a choice at all. So just really a difference between what's egosentonic versus what's egotistonic. So Dr. McKay, we've talked a little bit about some of the manifestations, but there are different subtypes of OCD, right?
迷思和误解。但我认为最大的一点是，人们认为强迫症患者喜欢他们正在做的事情。所以当人们说“我在清洁方面太强迫症了”或者“我在整理东西或追求完美方面太强迫症了”，第一，这在语法上又是错误的。但第二，这也暗示了我喜欢某种方式，我需要它那样，因为我真的非常喜欢它。而强迫症患者讨厌他们正在做的事情。他们根本不想做他们正在做的事情，他们不想去想他们正在做的事情，这根本不是一种选择。所以这确实是“顺应强迫”（ego-syntonic）与“反强迫”（ego-dystonic）之间的区别。那么麦凯博士，我们已经谈到了一些表现形式，但强迫症有不同的亚型，对吧？

